{
  "slug": "claude-video-vision",
  "name": "Claude Video Vision",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A perception layer that gives Claude Code the ability to watch and understand videos. Extracts frames via ffmpeg and processes audio through multiple configurable backends (Gemini API, local Whisper, or OpenAI Whisper API). Claude receives the frames as images plus an audio transcription with timestamps and reasons about them together. Includes an interactive setup wizard, adaptive extraction (fps, resolution, and time ranges automatically adjust to the user's question), and auto-download of Whisper models. 100% free and open source.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, **1 agent**, **2 commands** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `video-perception` (Use when the user mentions a video file (.mp4, .mov, .avi, .mkv, .webm), a YouTube URL, asks to…)\n- **Agents** (1): `frame-describer` (Describes video frames as detailed text)\n- **Commands** (2): `setup-video-vision` (Interactive setup wizard for claude-video-vision — configure backend, whisper, frames, and verify dependencies), `watch-video` (Watch and analyze a video file or YouTube URL — extracts frames and audio for understanding)\n- **MCP servers** (1): `claude-video-vision`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install claude-video-vision@claude-community` from `jordanrendric/claude-video-vision`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 1,
    "agent": 1,
    "command": 2,
    "mcp": 1
  },
